1. What is a framework
  • A predefined structure that organizes your code
  • Handles common backend tasks (routing, requests, responses)

2. Why it’s important
  • You don’t build everything from scratch
  • Gives structure to your API
  • Lets you focus on business logic

3. Basic structure of FastAPI

Core components:

1. App (entry point)
  • Central object
  • All routes are attached here

2. Routes (endpoints)
  • Map URL → function
  • Example:
    • /users
    • /validate

3. Function (logic)
  • Runs when route is called
  • Handles processing

4. Models (data structure)
  • Define expected input/output
  • Used for validation

Minimal structure:
  • App
    ├── Routes
    │     └── Functions
    │             └── Models

Request flow:
  • Client → Route → Function → Response
